counterfactuals.output:
A method of fabricating a device, the method comprising:

1. providing an inner electrode comprising an electron-conducting or semiconducting material M1;

2. providing a hollow insulating support comprising material M6, the hollow insulating support defining an internal passage configured to receive the inner electrode;

3. depositing a conductive material M2 on at least a portion of the hollow insulating support;

4. forming a plurality of insulating colloidal particles comprising material M3;

5. depositing a conductive material M4 and a layer L1 comprising material M5, such that the conductive material M4 and the layer L1 are disposed in operative relation to the insulating colloidal particles;

6. inserting the inner electrode into the internal passage of the hollow insulating support;

7. stabilizing one or more end regions of the resulting structure with material M7; and

8. removing one or more sacrificial materials to form the fabricated device.
